In this task another micro service tenant_service will be created.
The micro service will
    - Use auth-client-lib for JWT token exploring and setting security context holder using JwtAuthenticationFilter
    - The End points will be PreAuthorized by permission
    - Keep similarities with the auth_service architecture
    - Generate the Dockerfile as generated in auth_service
    - Add this micro service in docker-compose too
    - Use available port number
    - Use exception handling similarly they are handled in auth_service
    - Use the Swagger and also write comments properly

 Rest End Point:
 ===============
 1. Tenant Fees Controller
 =============================
      Endpoints:
       - CRUD end points with TENANT_PAYMENT_APPROVAL(Management) and TENANT_PAYMENT_VIEW (Search, list and view) permission accordingly
       - search and list productCount in range of productCountFrom, productCountTo
       - search and list by packageCode

 2. Tenant Registration Controller
 =================================
      Endpoints:
      - Tenant's registration request endpoint will be allowed publicly
      - List all Tenant Registration Requests (TENANT_PAYMENT_VIEW or TENANT_PAYMENT_APPROVAL Permission will require)
      - List all Tenant Registration Requests filtered by ID, packageCode, tenantBusinessName partial search, approvalStatus, domainPrefix, contactNumber (search in both contactNumber1 and contactNumber2), emailAddress(TENANT_PAYMENT_VIEW or TENANT_PAYMENT_APPROVAL Permission will require)
      - View a Tenant Registration Requests by ID (TENANT_PAYMENT_VIEW or TENANT_PAYMENT_APPROVAL Permission will require)
      - Endpoint to check whether the domainPrefix is allocated or used already or not (No permission needed)
      - Tenant's registration request Approval/Reject with TENANT_PAYMENT_APPROVAL permission, After Approval tenant will be created and inserted in tenant_info with Active status